<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tashkent</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chach, Shash</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tashkent is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, in an oasis watered by the Chirchiq river. Known in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> as Chach or Shash, it was a trading city between the farmland of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> and the steppe. Taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1865, it became the capital of Russian Turkestan and then of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> SSR from 1930. After an earthquake in 1966 much of the city was rebuilt.</p></div>
